From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:11:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] obj.cc: stop calling _PySys_GetSizeOf() on Python 3.13+

_obj::get_sizeof() (used by Frame.__sizeof__ to account for the column
names tuple and dict) calls _PySys_GetSizeOf(). Python 3.13 moved that
function to the internal C API (Include/internal/pycore_sysmodule.h), so
the extension no longer compiles:

  src/core/python/obj.cc: error: '_PySys_GetSizeOf' was not declared
  in this scope

This is the reason datatable 1.1.0 cannot be built for cp313/cp314.
On 3.13+ call sys.getsizeof() through the public API instead, which is
what _PySys_GetSizeOf() implements (__sizeof__ plus the GC header), so
the reported sizes are unchanged. Older interpreters keep the original
call.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [upstream has merged no external code change since the 1.1.0 release]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 src/core/python/obj.cc | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/core/python/obj.cc b/src/core/python/obj.cc
index 6e9a228..75e99cb 100644
--- a/src/core/python/obj.cc
+++ b/src/core/python/obj.cc
@@ -1191,7 +1191,18 @@ std::string _obj::typestr() const {
 
 
 size_t _obj::get_sizeof() const {
+#if PY_VERSION_HEX >= 0x030D0000
+  // _PySys_GetSizeOf() is internal API as of Python 3.13
+  PyObject* getsizeof = PySys_GetObject("getsizeof");
+  if (!getsizeof) return static_cast<size_t>(-1);
+  PyObject* res = PyObject_CallOneArg(getsizeof, v);
+  if (!res) return static_cast<size_t>(-1);
+  size_t size = PyLong_AsSize_t(res);
+  Py_DECREF(res);
+  return size;
+#else
   return _PySys_GetSizeOf(v);
+#endif
 }
 
 size_t _obj::get_refcount() const {
